cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "THEIA: grounded radiogenomic prediction of EGFR status from lung CT"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Loke
    given-names: Sathvik
repository-code: "https://github.com/sathvikloke/THEIA"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A vision-language model that predicts EGFR mutation status from lung CT while
  supervising its attention against tumour segmentations. On NSCLC-Radiogenomics
  (153 labelled patients, 40 EGFR-mutant) it reaches a pooled out-of-fold AUC of
  0.627 +/- 0.041 across seeds. Reported alongside it, and central to
  interpreting it: smoking status alone reaches 0.794, a logistic regression on
  frozen features matches the full model on identical folds, and adding the
  model on top of five clinical variables changes AUC by -0.022 +/- 0.027 with
  every seed's confidence interval including zero. See docs/RESULTS.md.
keywords:
  - radiogenomics
  - non-small cell lung cancer
  - EGFR
  - weakly supervised localisation
  - reproducibility
